{"name":"Rosy Copper","hex":"#cf8974","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Rose-coloured.","Of any reddish hue from bright pink to the color of ruddy cheeks in a light-skinned person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make pinkish in colour.","To present in a deceptively optimistic or positive light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosy"},{"term":"copper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reddish-brown metallic chemical element (symbol Cu) with the atomic number 29; also, the metal made up of this element.","The reddish-brown colour of copper (etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of copper (etymology 1, noun sense 1).","Having the reddish-brown colour of copper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosy","blocks":[{"text":"Rosy is a given name or nickname and, more rarely, a surname. It may refer to:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosy"},{"title":"Copper","blocks":[{"text":"Copper is a chemical element; it has symbol Cu and atomic number 29. It is a soft, malleable, and ductile metal with very high thermal and electrical conductivity. A freshly exposed surface of pure copper has a pinkish-orange color. Copper is used as a conductor of heat and electricity, as a building material, and as a constituent of various metal alloys, such as sterling silver used in jewelry, cupronickel used to make marine hardware and coins, and constantan used in strain gauges and thermocouples for temperature measurement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/NatCopper.jpg/330px-NatCopper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL